{
	title: 'host.ts split into cohesive modules',
	spec: "src/host/host.ts is no longer than 400 lines (task 0j) and its code lives in several host modules, each with one job and its own exported object per the module conventions (tasks/README.md). host.test.ts follows the split, so each module's tests sit next to it (tests have no size limit, but a 1000-line test file is as hard to read as a 1000-line module). The split is decided from the code as it is when this task runs, not planned ahead: read host.ts, group functions by the state they touch and by who calls them, and cut along those seams. A module that only forwards calls to another is a sign of a bad cut. Behaviour and the protocol do not change. Names that other modules, local.ts overrides, eval and tests rely on either stay on the `host` object or move with every caller in the same commit. Take host.ts off the size exception list. The whole suite passes before and after with no test weakened or deleted, except tests that moved.",
